THIS THIS IS THE NEWS - May 2026 - THE NEWS IS THIS THIS
--------------------------------------------------------
  (Urrrrrgh, where am I? Wait... Wut!?!? It's 2026!?!?)

New features for Wav Composer Not Toilet!

Autogrouping
------------
Autogrouping introduces an easier way of adding modules to a group.
Instead of the creation of modules and then grouping then as a two step
process, autogrouping groups the modules as they're created.

    * Simpler syntax than the group data object.
    * Less work to keep track of modules which need to be added to
      (or removed from) a group.
    * Quicker and easier to introduce to or remove from a file
    * Allows modules to be added to new and/or existing groups.

The concept of directives was introduced to make this happen, with three
for the autogrouping process: autogroup_create, autogroup_add, and
autogroup_stop. The name of the group must be specified alongside each
of them.

    // example:
    autogroup_create group1
        constant one value 1.0 one
    autogroup_stop group1

    // something else here...

    autogroup_add
    group1
        constant_freq cf value 440.0 cf

        multiplier
        m
            in_signal1 one out_output
            in_signal2 cf out_output
        m
    group1

autogroup_stop is optional to explicilty specify, but must be triggered
by using the name of the group instead, which makes the syntax of
autogroup definitions in keeping with modules and data objects.

See tests/autogroup.wc for a simple example, and examples/bounce2.wc
for more a complex examples.


Entry Points
------------
The concept of entry points arises from the wish to create a voice part
in a file which can then be reused by multiple other files. Modules in
the voice part connect to the entry point, and then when that voice part
is used, the entry point is connected up appropriately.

For multi-layered voice parts, this concept dramatically reduces the
number of inputs requiring reconnection.

It's not exactly a new feature, the pieces were in place - wcnt_trigger
and wcnt_signal modules.

However, due to the way these modules work (wcnt_trigger actually does
nothing at all in the main processing loop), and the fact I had never
thought to use them in this way, the way the logic of how connections
are formed didn't accommodate all this, which created an error saying
outputs didn't exist when they do!

The fix was to postpone these connections until... they were ready.

---jwm/9th May 2026


THIS IS THE NEWS - February 2014 - THE NEWS IS THIS

     **** Wav Composer Not Toilet 1.30.0 ****


                   [:::>  <:::]      /---O
         .----------   wcnt   ---------- /
             Wav Composer Not Toilet!
        / ----------  1.30.0  ----------'
        O---/     [::> ROTL <::]

     The runt of the litter for command line
       modular audio synthesis in Linux!

After a break of five years from wcnt development
I took it up again - just in time to celebrate
wcnt's tenth anniversary. Intending simply to get
it building again on modern Linux systemts (3.10!)
something else happened instead...

    * Complete overhaul of the UI code for handling
      inputs and parameters to allow:
        * arbitrary ordering of items
        * optional items
        * optional groups of items
        * multiple choice items
        * self connection of optional inputs

    * Added descriptions of modules, data objects,
      inputs, outputs, and parameters for display
      by command line help.

    * New modules:
        * seq_echo      } these provide dedicated
        * seq_router    } routing of sequencer events
        * wcnt_note     }

    * Removed mono version of C* Plate plugin
    * Improved handling of LADSPA ports and
      validation of values specified for parameters
      (control ports in LADSPA terminology).

    * Removed pointless in_bar_trig from modules
      which used it to tell them when to check
      their bar number input (wavfile_out,
      serial_wavout, and fader modules).

    * Added time_is_relative parameter to toggle
      the interpretation of timings in the timer
      module.

    * Added recycle_mode parameter to timer to
      allow it to loop endlessly.

    * Added out_count output to pattern_trig to
      increment at each trigger output in the
      pattern - until the pattern starts over that
      is.

    * Changed the input/output/parameter names of
      the inspector module to perhaps make sense
      to those people who are not me.

    * Fixes for serial_wavout. say no more.

    * Fixes for fader to no longer ignore or
      forget about early fade-outs.

    * Added out_count output (a count of things)
      to fader to exist alongside out_bar output
      (a count of occurrences).

    * Fixed data object help.

    * Fixed sanity_checks to detect
      inconsistencies between set/get_param values
      like it was supposed to (and fixed the
      inconsistencies it found).

    * Removed compilation warnings

    * Fixes for compilation issues on modern
      systems.

Download the tarball, extract the code, cd into it, and make examples.

